# Playbook: questions

The form of every question you put to the owner (`AGENTS.md` → `Communication`), also a question a skill prescribes, and of a long message. Read it before you ask the owner a question and before a message of several items.

## One question

```text
❓ **Folder**: Where should the note go?
- a) `projects/course`
- b) `resources/prompt-engineering`

➡️ b) `resources/prompt-engineering` — the article is general, not for the course.
```

- The first line is `❓`, a bold title, a colon and the question; a long question may take several paragraphs.
- Two or more options are always an `a)`, `b)`, `c)` list, never inline with "or".
- Exactly one `➡️` line: the letter and the text of the option, then the reason in a few words. Word the question so that "yes" accepts the recommendation.
- A question with no options (an open answer): the `➡️` line holds your proposal and its reason.

## Several questions

```text
❓ **1. Folder**: Where should the note go?
- a) `projects/course`
- b) `resources/prompt-engineering`

➡️ b) `resources/prompt-engineering` — the article is general, not for the course.

❓ **2. Tag**: Which tag should the note get?
- a) the existing `topic/prompt-engineering`
- b) a new `topic/llm-evaluation`

➡️ a) `topic/prompt-engineering` — an existing tag of the same meaning beats a new one.
```

- Each question is the full block above: the question, its option list, its `➡️` line. A blank line stands between blocks and a number before each title. The questions, their options and their recommendations are never joined into one line or one block.
- A message with one question has no number. In a planning interview the numbers of the questions run on across rounds to the end of the task; the owner answers "1. b 2. a".

Done when each question of the message is its own block with a number, an option list and one `➡️` line.

## A short question

A question of one sentence, up to 120 characters, whose options need no context, drops only its title. Its options, its `➡️` line and, among several questions, its number stay:

```text
❓ Why do you save this?

➡️ Without an answer, I save it with no reason (—).
```

Among several questions the first line is `❓ **2.** Why do you save this?`. A longer question, or one whose options need context, keeps its title.

## A question with no recommendation

When no option can be recommended (a name, a reason only the owner knows), the `➡️` line says what you do without an answer:

```text
❓ **Project name**: What should the project be called?

➡️ Without an answer, I use the folder's name, `my-notes`.
```

An approval of a plan is a short question with no recommended option: the yes is the owner's alone.

```text
❓ Do you approve this plan?
- a) yes
- b) change it (tell me what)

➡️ Without an answer, I change nothing.
```

## A long message

In a message of several items, bold each item's label and the few words that matter. Bold no whole sentence:

```text
- **Note:** the article on prompt evaluation, saved to `resources/prompt-engineering`.
- **Source:** the author's blog, read last week.
- **Status:** the commit is **not pushed** and **needs your approval**.
- **Tag:** **missing**; the existing `topic/prompt-engineering` fits.
```

Done when each item of a long message starts with a bold label and no sentence is bold as a whole.
